{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"title":"Hypergraph","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph.swift#L39","fileName":"Hypergraph.swift"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set of vertices of any size, the empty set included (Berge, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hypergraphs"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", 1989). Not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and no shared parent with one: a hyperedge is not an edge. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidenceGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads a hypergraph as its bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how the graph algorithms reach it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Associated-Types","generated":true,"title":"Associated Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/Hyperedges-swift.ass